  {
    "id": "1ed8306d8739b54bebb5",
    "sourceHash": "1ed8306d8739b54bebb5fa1cd97870286f90cc27e400d0b1e1872a92f9af21de",
    "th": "Dodge, Dash, Disengage, Hide, Help, Grapple, Shove, Ready, Search, Use an Object, and escaping a grapple go through take_action, never through narration alone: the server spends the action, rolls the contest a grapple, shove or escape needs against the real stats, and applies the result (a dodging character is genuinely harder to hit, a grappled enemy genuinely cannot move). A grapple or shove replaces one attack of the Attack action, so a character with Extra Attack can still swing after it. Pass bonus: true only when a feature makes it a bonus action (a rogue's Cunning Action Dash, Disengage or Hide, Expeditious Retreat's Dash, a Thief's Fast Hands Use an Object); a monk's Patient Defense, Step of the Wind and Flurry of Blows are use_resource Ki with that variant, which spends the ki and the bonus action. Help with targetEnemyId helps an attack on that creature (the helper within 5 feet of it); Help with none helps an ability check. Ready takes the trigger in words and commits to ONE action: an attack unless readied names another (move, help, use_object, item, stabilize, feature, or any other take_action action); when you judge the trigger has come, release exactly that action off their turn with its own tool (pc_attack for an attack, move_token for a move, take_action, use_item, stabilize or use_resource for the rest): the server spends their reaction and refuses any other action or a second release. While a character holds a readied action, enemy_attack does not walk an enemy that is out of reach: move it with move_token, release the readied action if its trigger fired, then attack.",
    "status": "technical",
    "reviewed": true,
    "reason": "AI-only tool schema/name or internal prompt contract; not rendered to players. Preserve canonical English."
  },
